module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.InternalHom.CurryingHomEquiv

/-! # The cochain-level evaluation morphism on homogeneous local sections

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `A`, `B`, `D` be complexes of `O`-modules.  The currying
bijection of Stacks 0A90 on morphism groups,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryHomEquiv`, and its value at the identity, the cochain-level
evaluation morphism `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.cochainEvaluation`, are both obtained by
conjugating the isomorphism of complexes of Stacks 0A90 with the two global descriptions of
Tag 0A8Z.  Neither had a formula on local sections.

This file supplies it.  The total tensor complex is generated by the local pure tensors
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.tensorComplexSection`, so a morphism out of it is pinned down by
its values on them, and the formulas below are what pins these two morphisms down:

* the transpose of `f : A ⟶ SheafHom(B, D)` takes the local pure tensor of `a` and `l` to the
  value on `l` of the Hom section `f(a)`;
* in particular the evaluation morphism takes the local pure tensor of a local section `ξ` of
  `SheafHom(B, D)` and a local section `l` of `B` to `ξ(l)`, with no sign and no restriction.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryCochainEquiv_v_app_tensorComplexSection`: the curried
  cochain of a degree-`n` cochain `z : A ⟶ SheafHom(B, D)` takes the local pure tensor of `a` and
  `l` to `z(a)(l)` — currying of cochains on homogeneous local sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryHomEquiv_val_app_tensorComplexSection`: the same for the
  transpose of a morphism of complexes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.cochainEvaluation_val_app_tensorComplexSection`: **the
  cochain-level evaluation morphism on homogeneous local sections**, `ξ ⊗ l ↦ ξ(l)`.

## Nothing here is tagged

Tag 0A90 is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafHomTensorCurryIso`, which carries the tag, and the
bijection of morphism groups read off it is a step of the proof of Tag 0GM7, not a clause of any
published statement.  No declaration here carries a tag.

## Implementation notes

*Why this is not immediate from the local construction.*  The currying isomorphism of complexes
is given on local sections by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryFun`, whose defining property
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.applyHomSectionOver_curryFun` already is a formula on local pure
tensors.  What stands between that and `curryHomEquiv` is the detour through global sections:
`curryHomEquiv` is the degree-zero global *cocycle* form of the isomorphism, so a cochain on the
one side is a global section of the internal Hom complex on the other, and the two are matched by
the `globalSectionsIso` field of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.SheafHomComplex`.  The bridge is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafHomComplex_globalSectionsIso_v_app`: the cochain a global
section determines has, at each object of the site, the same values as the cochain its sections
over that object determine.  Applied twice — once to read the given cochain `z` off the global
section it corresponds to, once to read the conclusion off the image of that section — it turns
the formula for `curryFun` into the formula for `curryCochainEquiv`.

*The intermediate degree is a variable.*  The degree `q` of the Hom section `z(a)` is carried as
a variable with `t + n = q` rather than written `t + n`, exactly as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryRule_degree` does, so that the `n = 0` instance used for
`curryHomEquiv` can take `q = t` without an `Int` arithmetic crossing inside a section type.

*The restriction arrow is the identity.*  `applyHomSectionOver_curryFun` is stated over an
arbitrary arrow `g : W ⟶ U` of the site; here `U = W` and `g = 𝟙 W`, because the cochain of a
*global* section is read object by object through `Over.mk (𝟙 W)`.  That is also why the values
below are `applyHomSection` rather than `applyHomSectionOver`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A90](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A90)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A8Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A8Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GM7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GM7)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite CochainComplex.HomComplex

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

universe u

attribute [local instance] ringSheafSectionsCommRing presheafOfModulesMonoidalCategory
  ringSheafOverSectionsCommRing

/-- A degree of an isomorphism of complexes of abelian groups is an isomorphism, read on an
element.  Stated here over an abstract complex shape so that the step is one
`Iso.inv_hom_id_apply` and not a rewrite inside a complex of global sections. -/
private lemma iso_f_inv_hom_apply {c : ComplexShape ℤ}
    {P Q : HomologicalComplex AddCommGrpCat.{u} c} (e : P ≅ Q) (n : ℤ) (y : Q.X n) :
    AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom (e.hom.f n) (AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom (e.inv.f n) y) = y :=
  ((HomologicalComplex.eval AddCommGrpCat c n).mapIso e).inv_hom_id_apply y

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} X.O).Additive]
  [∀ A, ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} X.O).obj A).Additive]
  [∀ (K₁ K₂ : HomologicalComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u,
    u} X.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)),
    HomologicalComplex.HasMapBifunctor K₁ K₂ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O)
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)]
  (A B D : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ)

/-- The formula for currying on homogeneous local sections, stated at an arbitrary degree-`n`
global section `s` of `SheafHom(A, SheafHom(B, D))` whose cochain is `z`.

`s` is a variable, and the two global descriptions of Tag 0A8Z appear only through
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafHomComplex_globalSectionsIso_v_app`, which is what keeps the
whole argument inside the section spelling: the identification of `s` with the preimage of `z`
is supplied by the caller and is never rewritten under
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryCochainEquiv`. -/
private lemma curry_v_app_tensorComplexSection_of_globalSection (n : ℤ)
    (z : Cochain A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj n)
    (s : (globalSectionsComplex X (sheafHomComplex X A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj).obj).X n)
    (hsz : AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom
        ((sheafHomComplex X A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj).globalSectionsIso.hom.f n) s =
      ULift.up z)
    (c d t r q : ℤ) (hcd : c + n = d) (htr : t + r = c) (htq : t + n = q) (hrq : r + q = d)
    (W : X.C) (a : (A.X t).val.obj (op W)) (l : (B.X r).val.obj (op W)) :
    ((AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom
          ((sheafHomComplex X (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.tensorComplex X.O).obj A).obj B)
            D).globalSectionsIso.hom.f n)
          (AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom
            ((globalSectionsComplexMap X (sheafHomTensorCurryIso X A B D).hom).f n)
            s)).down.v c d hcd).val.app (op W) (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr a l) =
      applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W q r d hrq
        ((z.v t q htq).val.app (op W) a) l := by
  -- Reading `z` off `s`: the local section of `SheafHom(A, SheafHom(B, D))` over `W` given by `s`
  -- evaluates by `z`.
  have hz : applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj) W n t q htq
        (s.val (op W)) a =
      ((z.v t q htq).val.app (op W)) a := by
    refine (sheafHomComplex_globalSectionsIso_v_app X A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj n t q htq
      s W a).symm.trans ?_
    rw [hsz]
  rw [sheafHomComplex_globalSectionsIso_v_app, globalSectionsComplexMap_val]
  change applyHomSectionOver X
      (sheafHomComplex X (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.tensorComplex X.O).obj A).obj B) D) W W
        (𝟙 W) n c d hcd
      (curryFun X W (s.val (op W))) (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr a l) = _
  rw [applyHomSectionOver_curryFun X W (s.val (op W)) c d hcd t r htr (𝟙 W) a l,
    ← curryRule_degree X W (s.val (op W)) t r d q htq hrq (𝟙 W) a l]
  exact congrArg (fun y => applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W q r d hrq y l) hz

/-- **Currying of cochains on homogeneous local sections.**  For a degree-`n` cochain
`z : A ⟶ SheafHom(B, D)`, the curried degree-`n` cochain `Tot(A ⊗_O B) ⟶ D` takes the local pure
tensor of a degree-`t` section `a` of `A` and a degree-`r` section `l` of `B` over an object `W`
of the site to the value on `l` of the degree-`q` Hom section `z(a)`, with no sign.

Together with `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.homSection_tensor_ext` — the total tensor complex is
generated by its local pure tensors — this pins `curryCochainEquiv` down. -/
theorem curryCochainEquiv_v_app_tensorComplexSection (n : ℤ)
    (z : Cochain A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj n)
    (c d t r q : ℤ) (hcd : c + n = d) (htr : t + r = c) (htq : t + n = q) (hrq : r + q = d)
    (W : X.C) (a : (A.X t).val.obj (op W)) (l : (B.X r).val.obj (op W)) :
    ((curryCochainEquiv X A B D n z).v c d hcd).val.app (op W)
        (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr a l) =
      applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W q r d hrq
        ((z.v t q htq).val.app (op W) a) l :=
  curry_v_app_tensorComplexSection_of_globalSection X A B D n z _
    (iso_f_inv_hom_apply (sheafHomComplex X A (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj).globalSectionsIso n
      (ULift.up z))
    c d t r q hcd htr htq hrq W a l

/-- **The transpose of a morphism of complexes on homogeneous local sections.**  For
`f : A ⟶ SheafHom(B, D)`, the transpose `Tot(A ⊗_O B) ⟶ D` of Stacks 0A90 takes the local pure
tensor of a degree-`t` section `a` of `A` and a degree-`r` section `l` of `B` over `W` to the
value on `l` of the Hom section `f(a)`. -/
theorem curryHomEquiv_val_app_tensorComplexSection (f : A ⟶ (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj)
    (c t r : ℤ) (htr : t + r = c) (hrt : r + t = c) (W : X.C)
    (a : (A.X t).val.obj (op W)) (l : (B.X r).val.obj (op W)) :
    ((curryHomEquiv X A B D f).f c).val.app (op W)
        (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr a l) =
      applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W t r c hrt ((f.f t).val.app (op W) a) l := by
  rw [curryHomEquiv_f, curryCochainEquiv_v_app_tensorComplexSection X A B D 0 (Cochain.ofHom f)
    c c t r t (add_zero c) htr (add_zero t) hrt W a l, Cochain.ofHom_v]

/-- **The cochain-level evaluation morphism of Tag 0A90 on homogeneous local sections.**  The
morphism `Tot(SheafHom(B, D) ⊗_O B) ⟶ D` takes the local pure tensor of a degree-`t` section `ξ`
of `SheafHom(B, D)` and a degree-`r` section `l` of `B` over an object `W` of the site to the
value `ξ(l)`: no sign, no restriction, no intervening identification.

This is the chain-level model of the evaluation whose class the derived bijection of Stacks 08DI
is compared against in
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.evaluationSquare_of_curryingSquare_kFlatResolution`. -/
theorem cochainEvaluation_val_app_tensorComplexSection
    (c t r : ℤ) (htr : t + r = c) (hrt : r + t = c) (W : X.C)
    (ξ : ((sheafHomComplex X B D).obj.X t).val.obj (op W))
    (l : (B.X r).val.obj (op W)) :
    ((cochainEvaluation X B D).f c).val.app (op W)
        (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr ξ l) =
      applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W t r c hrt ξ l := by
  rw [cochainEvaluation, curryHomEquiv_val_app_tensorComplexSection X
    (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj B D (𝟙 _) c t r htr hrt W ξ l, HomologicalComplex.id_f]
  rfl

/-! ### The formulas are characterisations -/

/-- **A morphism of complexes out of the total tensor complex is determined by its values on the
homogeneous local pure tensors.**

The currying bijection of Stacks 0A90 is surjective, so such a morphism is the transpose of some
`g : A ⟶ SheafHom(B, D)`; its values on the local pure tensors are the values of the Hom sections
`g(a)`, by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.curryHomEquiv_val_app_tensorComplexSection`; and a local
section of the internal Hom complex is determined by its values
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.homSection_ext`). -/
theorem tensorComplexSection_hom_ext
    {e e' : (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.tensorComplex X.O).obj A).obj B) ⟶ D}
    (h : ∀ (c t r : ℤ) (htr : t + r = c) (W : X.C)
      (a : (A.X t).val.obj (op W)) (l : (B.X r).val.obj (op W)),
      (e.f c).val.app (op W) (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr a l) =
        (e'.f c).val.app (op W) (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr a l)) :
    e = e' := by
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := (curryHomEquiv X A B D).surjective e
  obtain ⟨g', rfl⟩ := (curryHomEquiv X A B D).surjective e'
  refine congrArg (fun y => curryHomEquiv X A B D y)
    (HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun t ↦ SheafOfModules.hom_ext (PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
      fun W ↦ ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun a ↦ ?_)))
  obtain ⟨W⟩ := W
  refine homSection_ext X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W t fun r q hrq V i l ↦ ?_
  rw [applyHomSectionOver_restrict, applyHomSectionOver_restrict,
    ← PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (g.f t).val i.op a,
    ← PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (g'.f t).val i.op a,
    ← curryHomEquiv_val_app_tensorComplexSection X A B D g q t r (by omega) hrq V
      ((A.X t).val.map i.op a) l,
    ← curryHomEquiv_val_app_tensorComplexSection X A B D g' q t r (by omega) hrq V
      ((A.X t).val.map i.op a) l]
  exact h q t r (by omega) V ((A.X t).val.map i.op a) l

/-- **The local-section formula characterises the cochain-level evaluation morphism.**  A
morphism of complexes `Tot(SheafHom(B, D) ⊗_O B) ⟶ D` that takes every homogeneous local pure
tensor `ξ ⊗ l` to `ξ(l)` is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.cochainEvaluation`.

This is what lets a candidate chain-level model of the evaluation of Stacks 08DI be identified
with the evaluation morphism of Tag 0A90: it is enough to compute the candidate on homogeneous
local pure tensors. -/
theorem eq_cochainEvaluation_of_val_app_tensorComplexSection
    (e : (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.tensorComplex X.O).obj
        (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj).obj B) ⟶ D)
    (he : ∀ (c t r : ℤ) (htr : t + r = c) (hrt : r + t = c) (W : X.C)
      (ξ : ((sheafHomComplex X B D).obj.X t).val.obj (op W))
      (l : (B.X r).val.obj (op W)),
      (e.f c).val.app (op W) (tensorComplexSection X t r c htr ξ l) =
        applyHomSection X (sheafHomComplex X B D) W t r c hrt ξ l) :
    e = cochainEvaluation X B D :=
  tensorComplexSection_hom_ext X (sheafHomComplex X B D).obj B D
    fun c t r htr W ξ l ↦ (he c t r htr (by omega) W ξ l).trans
      (cochainEvaluation_val_app_tensorComplexSection X B D c t r htr (by omega) W ξ l).symm

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
